stop to think about the accuracy of the information and how it might be
used. Sometimes it's inaccurate, sometimes it isn't.

Am I the one who killed the Kennedys? ("Afterall it was you and me," says
Mick). Or maybe I am the one who gave the secret of the A-bomb to the red
nasties. Maybe I am the one who gave Pollard the keys to our subs.  Or
maybe I'm that cop knocking at your back door . . . If a dossier says so,
so what? What can be done? By whom? To whom? ("Arm yourself when the Frog
God smiles.")

There's nothing new here. Everytime we stick a toe in the ocean we enter
the food chain at a point much lower than our preferred landlubber position
at the top. Who knows where any one of us will be in cyberspace, the
structure of its food chain and our role in the nutrient mix. Blacknet is
just a wakeup call for sleepwalkers.

